  "id": "DrugBank_DB04572 - MONDO_18171",
  "verbalization": "Thiotepa, a chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the treatment of malignant germ cell tumors of the ovary through a chain of indications involving Altretamine. The evidence suggests that Thiotepa may be used in the context of immature ovarian teratomas, which in turn are linked to malignant dysgerminomatous germ cell tumors, both of which are classified as malignant germ cell tumors of the ovary. This pathway implies a potential role for Thiotepa in the management of this condition, possibly through its interaction with Altretamine, which is a known chemotherapeutic agent used in the treatment of these tumors. The overlapping indications across different paths highlight a possible mechanistic link between Thiotepa and the development or progression of malignant germ cell tumors of the ovary, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways with similar indications supports the hypothesis that Thiotepa may contribute to the treatment of this malignancy, though further research is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
